{"id":28115,"slug":"the-trial","title":"The Trial","year":1962,"country":"France, Italy, Yugoslavia","duration":118,"spine":1191,"url":"https://www.criterion.com/films/28115-the-trial","cover":"https://s3.amazonaws.com/criterion-production/films/709194f9d2983a7de56dbe73d112c255/lLNC4pN9sudu4N9SnppidWe30cS7Ci_large.jpg","description":"A feverishly inspired take on Franz Kafka’s novel, Orson Welles’s The Trial casts Anthony Perkins as the bewildered office drone Josef K., whose arrest for an unspecified crime plunges him into a menacing bureaucratic labyrinth of guilt, corruption, and paranoia. Exiled from Hollywood and creatively unchained, Welles poured his ire at the studio system, the blacklist, and all forms of totalitarian oppression into this cinematic statement—a bold, personal film that he himself considered one of his greatest. Dizzying camera angles, expressionistic lighting, increasingly surreal locations—Welles unleashed the full force of his visual brilliance to convey the nightmarish disorientation of a world gone mad.","boxset":0,"scraped":1,"directors":[{"name":"Orson Welles","slug":"orson-welles"}],"cast":[{"actor":"Anthony Perkins","role":"Josef K.","slug":"anthony-perkins"},{"actor":"Jeanne Moreau","role":"Marika Bürstner","slug":"jeanne-moreau"},{"actor":"Elsa Martinelli","role":"Hilda","slug":"elsa-martinelli"},{"actor":"Suzanne Flon","role":"Miss Pittl","slug":"suzanne-flon"},{"actor":"Madeleine Robinson","role":"Mrs. Grubach","slug":"madeleine-robinson"},{"actor":"Romy Schneider","role":"Leni","slug":"romy-schneider"},{"actor":"Orson Welles","role":"Albert Hastler, the advocate","slug":"orson-welles"},{"actor":"Max Buchsbaum","role":"Examining magistrate","slug":"max-buchsbaum"},{"actor":"Arnoldo Foà","role":"Inspector A","slug":"arnoldo-foa"},{"actor":"Jess Hahn","role":"Second assistant inspector","slug":"jess-hahn"},{"actor":"Thomas Holtzmann","role":"Bert, the law student","slug":"thomas-holtzmann"},{"actor":"Fernand Ledoux","role":"Chief c